# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Amplified Traders environment configuration
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. NEVER commit `.env`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Site
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3600"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_NAME="Amplified Traders"

# Auth — NOTHING to configure here. Sessions are opaque random tokens (32
# bytes) hashed with SHA-256 and stored server-side: there is no shared
# signing secret to set and no key to rotate. See lib/tokens.ts, lib/auth.ts.

# --- Phase 2+ (database) ---------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://amplifiedtraders:CHANGE_ME@localhost:5433/amplifiedtraders?schema=public"
# TEST_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://amplifiedtraders:CHANGE_ME@localhost:5433/amplifiedtraders_test?schema=public"

# --- Initial administrator (provisioned by `pnpm db:seed`) ------------------
# Set these, then run `pnpm db:seed` to create the SUPER_ADMIN. Re-running the
# seed never resets an existing admin's password.
# ADMIN_EMAIL="admin@amplifiedtraders.com"
# ADMIN_PASSWORD="ChangeMe-Admin-123!"
# ADMIN_NAME="Amplified Traders Admin"

# --- Integrations (optional — leave blank to disable) ----------------------
# SMTP: the only variable the code reads is SMTP_HOST. Until the transport is
# implemented, setting it does NOT make email work — messages are reported as
# not delivered rather than faked. See lib/notifications/email.ts.
#
# The deployment reads that honesty all the way to the member: while there is
# no transport, /forgot-password says so and points at the contact form instead
# of claiming a reset link has been sent. Flip TRANSPORT_IMPLEMENTED in
# lib/notifications/email.ts when a real transport lands.
# SMTP_HOST="" SMTP_PORT="587" SMTP_USER="" SMTP_PASSWORD=""
# EMAIL_FROM="Amplified Traders <no-reply@amplifiedtraders.com>"
# PAYMENTS_PROVIDER="" PAYMENTS_SECRET=""
# WHATSAPP_TOKEN="" TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=""
# KYC_PROVIDER="" KYC_SECRET=""

# --- Production only --------------------------------------------------------
# The variables the running app actually reads:
#   DATABASE_URL          REQUIRED. The app refuses to boot without it.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL  Baked into the bundle at build time. Set it BEFORE
#                          `pnpm build`, or every canonical URL, sitemap entry
#                          and email link points at the wrong origin.
#   SMTP_HOST             Optional. See above.
# The deploy script asserts DATABASE_URL is present before it deploys.

